      "source": [
        "### Introduction\n",
        "**Hook**\n",
        "\n",
        "Formula 1 is best known for its high-speed unpredictability, but how much of each race is predetermined before it even begins?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question**\n",
        "\n",
        "To what extent do drivers actually change positions during a race, or are race results mostly determined by their starting grid position?\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data Reveal**\n",
        "\n",
        "An analysis of Formula 1 race data from the 2021–2024 seasons shows a strong relationship between starting and finishing positions.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Surprise**\n",
        "\n",
        "Despite the expectation that races involve frequent and significant position changes, most drivers actually finish relatively close to where they started on the grid, reinforcing the strong link between qualifying position and race results.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Deeper Layer**\n",
        "\n",
        "However, the relationship is not absolute. Certain drivers consistently outperform their starting position, while others regularly fall behind it, showing that race execution still plays a meaningful role.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Conclusion of Question**\n",
        "\n",
        "Overall, qualifying position is a strong predictor of race outcome in Formula 1, but it does not fully determine the final result.\n",
        "\n",
        "<br><hr>"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "thaRqqv74eZP"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
